"I can't get my left foot up."

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.210
Anyway, it probably looked really awesome

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:21.540
and I turned America on with those moves.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.310
That was "Don't Worry, Baby."

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.040
In his memoir, Brian Wilson
wrote that he composed it

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.930
after hearing the Ronette
song "Be My Baby,"

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.060
which is also such a classic.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.260
He heard that for the first time

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.390
and apparently, he called
his lyricist right away

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.640
and within an hour of
the words being written,

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.990
Brian knew he had a hit.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.092
Did you hear it?

00:02:38.092 --> 00:02:39.000
(audience laughing)

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.650
Still sticking.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.230
I'm not going anywhere, okay?

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.880
Like, don't let her break her leg.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.230
Anyway, I love that song so much.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.480
I love the Beach Boys,
it's such a good vibe.

